# Intentionally no catch-all rewrite.
#
# The production build emits one flat <route>.html file per known EN/FR route
# plus a top-level 404.html. Cloudflare serves each flat file at its slashless
# route, matching the application's canonical URLs. Pages evaluates _redirects
# before asset matching, so a wildcard SPA rewrite would mask those prerendered
# documents, hashed assets, and the real 404 response.
#
# A database-only route added after the last build needs a new prerendered build
# or an explicit asset-first Pages Function/SSR implementation. Do not restore a
# wildcard rewrite to simulate support for that case.
